    {
      "SurveyID": "SV_1X34YGdTiaOe2G2",
      "Element": "SQ",
      "PrimaryAttribute": "QID80",
      "SecondaryAttribute": "Q4c7ad876212f200d-chunk_bdf35babea9313ce7e5f0eea",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<p><strong>EDOS Label</strong></p><p><strong>4.1 supporting mistreatment of individual women</strong> – Expressing support for mistreatment of women as individuals. Support can be shown by denying, understating, or seeking to justify such mistreatment.</p><br><p><strong>Paragraph</strong></p>2. Online experiences of gender-based harassment<br><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">PERCENTAGE OF GIRLS AND YOUNG WOMEN FACING DIFFERENT TYPES OF HARASSMENT\n\nPERCENTAGE OF GIRLS AND YOUNG WOMEN FACING DIFFERENT TYPES OF HARASSMENT\n\n</div><table>\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n        <th>Type of Harassment</th>\n        <th>Percentage</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n        <td>Racist comments</td>\n<td>29</td>\n    </tr>\n<tr>\n        <td>Stalking</td>\n<td>32</td>\n    </tr>\n<tr>\n        <td>Body shaming</td>\n<td>39</td>\n    </tr>\n<tr>\n        <td>Threats of physical violence</td>\n<td>21</td>\n    </tr>\n<tr>\n        <td>Abusive and insulting language</td>\n<td>59</td>\n    </tr>\n<tr>\n        <td>Threats of sexual violence</td>\n<td>39</td>\n    </tr>\n<tr>\n        <td>Purposeful embarrassment</td>\n<td>41</td>\n    </tr>\n<tr>\n        <td>Sexual harassment</td>\n<td>37</td>\n    </tr>\n<tr>\n        <td>Anti LGBTIQ+ Comments</td>\n<td>26</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">\n\nOf the girls who have been harassed, 47% have been threatened with physical or sexual violence.\nHarassment appears to fall into two specific categories:\nA. Harassment that girls experience simply for                B. A heightened level of harassment when girls are\nbeing a girl and for being online. It is unrelated to the     actively engaged in speaking out online. Activists\ncontent of what she posts and is ubiquitous to girls’         are attacked for what they are saying and for their\nexperiences of social media use. It gets worse if you         outspokenness. Harassers are interacting with the\nare Black, identify as LGBTIQ+ or have a disability.          content, with the debates girls and young women are\n                                                              involved in and the issues they raise.</div><br>",
        "DataExportTag": "Q4c7ad876212f200d-chunk_bdf35babea9313ce7e5f0eea",
        "QuestionType": "MC",
        "Selector": "SAVR",
